P = {
# ── oxygen_equality: generosity on the manifold ──
"quest_oxygen_equality_01": ("The air is thin on every deck, but the slums breathe last and least, and the proposal is simple: route fresh oxygen to the slum blocks first, at night, when the children sleep deepest. Engineering has drawn the line, and the line passes the command deck's door, and no one has said that part out loud yet.",
 "The route line is pinned to the council table, and it ends where the slum blocks begin, and the room has gone quiet at the wrong end of the line.",
 "Route the slums first.", "Refuse. The generator cannot take the load."),
"quest_oxygen_equality_02": ("The proposal moves: fresh oxygen to the sick wards, because thin air is a second illness, and the infirmary has presented the cough count. Engineering says the route is possible, and the cost is pressure on the upper decks, and the upper decks have started to speak, and the cough count is still on the table.",
 "The cough count sits on the council table, and no one has moved it, and the route line waits underneath.",
 "Route air to the sick wards.", "Refuse. The pressure drop touches everyone."),
"quest_oxygen_equality_03": ("The proposal names the worker decks: the people who run the shelter breathe last, because their decks are farthest from the manifold, and the route is drawn, and the engineer has written in the margin of her own plan that this is how it should have been built, and signed the note, which is unlike her.",
 "The engineer's margin note is passed around the room, and everybody reads the signature.",
 "Reroute to the worker decks.", "Leave the manifold as it stands."),
"quest_oxygen_equality_04": ("The proposal is short: fresh oxygen to the children's sector, because lungs that are still growing are being shaped by thin air, and the shape is in the infirmary's charts. The vote is called, and the room notices it has already decided, and the vote is held anyway, because votes matter.",
 "The growth charts hang on the wall, and the room has seen them, and the vote is called, and nobody is surprised by the sound of it.",
 "Route air to the children.", "Refuse. Every deck has charts."),
"quest_oxygen_equality_05": ("The proposal reaches the people no route was drawn for: the outcasts, down where the air is twice-recycled, and the engineering line is drawn to their door, and someone has asked what the outcasts will give in return, and the room has waited, and no answer came, and the asker has looked down.",
 "The route line ends at the outcasts' door, and the question what will they give hangs in the room, unanswered, while the asker studies the table.",
 "Route the air. No payment.", "Refuse. They have managed this long."),
"quest_oxygen_equality_06": ("The proposal names the refugees: the ones who came through the airlock last month breathe the shelter's thinnest air, in the rooms nobody else wanted, and the route is drawn, and the cost is listed, and someone has said they are not ours yet, and the room has gone very quiet, because the shelter remembers being at an airlock once.",
 "The room goes quiet at the words not ours yet, and the silence is still sitting there when the vote is called.",
 "Route air to the refugee rooms.", "Refuse. Ours first."),
"quest_oxygen_equality_07": ("The proposal is practical this time: fresh oxygen to the surface prep rooms, because the scouts go out breathing thin air and come back to thinner, and the route is cheap, and the scout lead has been asked to speak, and she has said we would notice, and sat down, and that is the entire testimony.",
 "The scout lead sits down after saying we would notice, and the room turns the route plan over in its hands.",
 "Route air to the prep rooms.", "Refuse. Scouts are built for worse."),
"quest_oxygen_equality_08": ("The proposal reaches the elder bunks, and the engineer has drawn the route herself, and in the margin she has written no arithmetic this time, only the names of the people who sleep there, and the first name is the man who laid the manifold's first pipe, and the room has noticed, because the room knows its own history when it is shown.",
 "The route plan goes around the table with names in the margin, and the first name is the man who laid the first pipe, and the room reads all of them.",
 "Route air to the elder bunks.", "Refuse. Let them keep the heat instead."),
"quest_oxygen_equality_09": ("The proposal is a single line on the manifold's own diagram: equalize all decks, because the shelter's air belongs to the shelter. Engineering says it can be done, and the cost is that every deck will feel it, and the proposal says that is the point, and the line has been read aloud twice, because nobody heard it right the first time.",
 "The manifold diagram hangs with the equalize line drawn across it, and the room has heard that is the point twice, and the vote is called.",
 "Equalize every deck.", "Refuse. Command keeps its margin."),
"quest_oxygen_equality_10": ("The final proposal is the one nobody wrote, so the engineer wrote it: Command gives up its pure-air loop, because the shelter breathes one air or it does not. The council has read it, and the room has waited, and what the room is waiting for is whether anyone on the council will speak first, and what they will say.",
 "The proposal sits in front of the council, and the room waits to see who speaks first, and what it will be.",
 "Give up the pure air. All of it.", "Refuse. Command breathes first."),
# ── hippocratic_vow: the Chief Surgeon draws the line ──
"quest_hippocratic_vow_01": ("Medical supplies are counted in doses now, and the Chief Surgeon has made her first demand: treat the mildly sick without hesitation, because small sicknesses are how big ones start, and the infirmary has learned this twice already. The demand is written in her hand, and her hand does not shake.",
 "The mildly sick line runs out the clinic door, and the Chief Surgeon stands at the head of it with the demand in her hand.",
 "Treat them. Spend the doses.", "Refuse. Save it for worse."),
"quest_hippocratic_vow_02": ("The demand continues: treat the badly injured without hesitation, even when the treatment costs more than the labor, because that is where arithmetic stops, she says, and she has said it to the council, and the council has shown her the arithmetic, and she has read it, and she has not changed her answer.",
 "The arithmetic sits on the table, and the Chief Surgeon has read it, and the room waits for the answer she has already given.",
 "Treat the badly injured.", "Refuse. The cost belongs to the shelter."),
"quest_hippocratic_vow_03": ("The demand reaches the chronic: the people whose treatment never ends and whose doses are counted forever, and the demand says treat without hesitation, because a shelter that counts its sick is counting something else, and she has not said what, and the room has heard it anyway.",
 "The chronic list is read aloud, and the list is long, and the Chief Surgeon has asked that it be read in full, and it is.",
 "Treat the chronic. All of them.", "Refuse. The doses do not stretch forever."),
"quest_hippocratic_vow_04": ("The demand names the elderly, and the council has asked what they return, and the Chief Surgeon has answered with a list of everything they built, and the list is two pages long, and she has read all of it, and the question has not been asked again.",
 "The two-page list sits on the council table, and the question about returns has not been asked again, and the vote is called.",
 "Treat the elderly.", "Refuse. Winter asks its own questions."),
"quest_hippocratic_vow_05": ("The demand is hardest this time: treat the terminal without hesitation, because the doses will not save them, which is not what the doses are for, she says, and the infirmary has gone quiet, because everyone in it knows what the doses are for, and nobody has said it out loud, and she has said it out loud.",
 "The Chief Surgeon has said what the doses are for, out loud, and the infirmary is still quiet, and the demand is on the table.",
 "Give them what they need.", "Refuse. The living come first."),
"quest_hippocratic_vow_06": ("The demand reaches the outsiders: the ones taken in from the ash, who owe the shelter nothing and are owed nothing, and the demand says treat without hesitation, because the clinic door is the one door that does not ask which side of it you were born on. The outsiders have been told to wait outside, and she has told them to wait inside, and the room has let her.",
 "The outsiders sit inside, because the Chief Surgeon said inside, and the room has let it stand.",
 "Treat the outsiders.", "Refuse. Our stock, our sick."),
"quest_hippocratic_vow_07": ("The demand has reached the line past the line: treat the enemies without hesitation, because three of them are in the infirmary now, from the raid, and they bleed the same, she says, and the room has looked at her, and she has said it again, slower, and nobody has answered.",
 "Three enemy wounded lie in the infirmary, and the room has looked at the Chief Surgeon, and she has said it again, slower, and the vote is not called yet.",
 "Treat them. They bleed the same.", "Refuse. They would not treat us."),
"quest_hippocratic_vow_08": ("The demand is one paragraph and the paragraph has a name in it: the condemned man in the brig is to be treated without hesitation, because he is bleeding, and because the shelter's sentence is the shelter's business and his blood is his. The room has divided, and the Chief Surgeon has taken her kit and stood by the door, and waits for the vote with her hand on the latch.",
 "The Chief Surgeon stands at the door with her kit, hand on the latch, and the vote is called with the room watching her hand.",
 "Let her treat him.", "Refuse. Let him bleed."),
"quest_hippocratic_vow_09": ("The demand is arithmetic now, and the arithmetic is hers: the last doses go to the lost causes, because that is what the word vow means, she says, and she has listed the lost causes by name, and the list is four names, and the room has heard them, and the room knows them, and the vote is not close and never was.",
 "Four names, read aloud, and the room knows all four, and the vote is called, and nobody counts hands.",
 "Spend the doses. All four.", "Refuse. Four names or forty winters."),
"quest_hippocratic_vow_10": ("The final demand is a single case: one life, tonight, that will take everything the infirmary has, and leave the shelter awake tomorrow with nothing, and the Chief Surgeon has not argued, she has only said the patient's name, and her age, and what she asked for this morning, and the room has not needed to vote, but it has voted, because the shelter should be able to say it chose.",
 "The Chief Surgeon has said the patient's name, and her age, and what she asked for this morning, and the room has voted anyway, because the shelter should be able to say it chose.",
 "Spend everything. Save her.", "Refuse. The shelter comes first."),
# ── forgiveness_doctrine: the brig empties one crime at a time ──
"quest_forgiveness_doctrine_01": ("The brig is full and the laws are harsh, and the Overseer has made a proposal the room does not expect: pardon the lazy, because the shelter has called laziness a crime since the first winter, and the brig holds people for it, and most of them are grieving, and the proposal says so, and the room has gone quiet at the word.",
 "The brig list is read aloud, and the word lazy has names under it, and most of the names are grieving, and the room has heard it said.",
 "Pardon the lazy.", "Refuse. The quota is the law."),
"quest_forgiveness_doctrine_02": ("The proposal continues: pardon the complainers, because the shelter has punished raised voices, and the voices were raised about water mostly, and the water was bad, and the proposal says so, in so many words, and the water crew has looked at their hands while it was read.",
 "The proposal says the water was bad, and the water crew looks at their hands while it is read, and nobody disagrees.",
 "Pardon the complainers.", "Refuse. Order comes first."),
"quest_forgiveness_doctrine_03": ("The proposal names the unlucky: pardon the accidental breakers, because the brig holds three people for things that broke in their hands, and the shelter knows, because everyone has broken something, and the proposal asks what the difference is between a hand and a crime, and nobody has an answer, and the vote is called.",
 "Three names for things that broke in their hands, and the room looks at its own hands, and the vote is called.",
 "Pardon the unlucky.", "Refuse. Broken things cost."),
"quest_forgiveness_doctrine_04": ("The proposal is hardest this time: pardon the food thieves, because every theft in the brig is a mouth, and every mouth belongs to the shelter, and the proposal says so, and the cook has stood up and said it is true, because he has caught two of them and reported one, and the room has heard the confession, and has not moved.",
 "The cook has confessed to the room, and the room has heard it, and nobody moves, and the proposal stands.",
 "Pardon the thieves.", "Refuse. Hunger is not a key."),
"quest_forgiveness_doctrine_05": ("The proposal reaches the ones who said no: pardon the insubordinate, because some of the orders they refused have since been refused by the whole room, and the proposal lists those orders, and the list is read aloud, and the room remembers each one, and the brig holds the people who said it first.",
 "The list of refused orders is read aloud, and the room remembers each one, and the brig holds the ones who said it first.",
 "Pardon the ones who said no.", "Refuse. Orders are orders."),
"quest_forgiveness_doctrine_06": ("The proposal names the hoarders, and the room has bristled, because hoarding is the crime the shelter feels, and the proposal has waited for the bristling to pass, and then read the list: what was hoarded, and why, and the why is mostly children, and the bristling has not gone away, but the vote is called anyway.",
 "The hoard list is read with its reasons, and the reasons are mostly children, and the room bristles and keeps bristling, and the vote is called.",
 "Pardon the hoarders.", "Refuse. The stores belong to the shelter."),
"quest_forgiveness_doctrine_07": ("The proposal reaches the deserters, and the room has gone quiet in a different way, because desertion is the crime the shelter fears, and the proposal has read the names, and where each one deserted from, and the places are ones the room has also wanted to leave, and the silence has lasted a long time.",
 "The desertion list is read with its places, and the places are ones the room knows, and the silence lasts a long time.",
 "Pardon the deserters.", "Refuse. The line has to hold."),
"quest_forgiveness_doctrine_08": ("The proposal is the one nobody wanted to hear: pardon the violent, and the room has stood up, part of it, and the proposal has waited, and then said the word carefully, and named the ones still in the brig for it, and two of the names have made people sit back down, and the room has watched itself do it.",
 "Part of the room has stood, and two of the names have made it sit back down, and the room has watched itself do it.",
 "Pardon the violent.", "Refuse. Some doors stay locked."),
"quest_forgiveness_doctrine_09": ("The proposal reaches the last crime: pardon the betrayers, and the room has not moved at all, which is how the room shows it is afraid, and the proposal has named the one betrayal in the brig, and the name is one the room loved, and the proposal has not argued, it has only asked the room to say, out loud, what it wants done.",
 "The name is said, and the room does not move, because the name is one the room loved, and the proposal waits for the room to speak.",
 "Pardon the betrayal.", "Refuse. Some things stay done."),
"quest_forgiveness_doctrine_10": ("The final proposal is a word the shelter has not used since before: amnesty, for all of them, because the brig is full and the laws are harsh and the community is a thing that heals or a thing that does not, and the Overseer has put the brig key on the table, and the room has looked at the key, and then at the room.",
 "The brig key sits on the council table, and the room looks at the key, and then at itself, and the vote is called.",
 "Open the brig. All of them.", "Refuse. The key stays on the table."),
# ── labor_relief: the shelter gives back what it took ──
"quest_labor_relief_01": ("The workers are breaking, and the proposal is on the table: eight-hour shifts, because the human body has a limit and the quota is a line, and only one of those is real. The foreman has presented the injury list, and the list is counted by hour, and the hour is the eleventh, and the room has looked at the arithmetic.",
 "The injury list is counted by hour, and the hour is the eleventh, and the room looks at the arithmetic, and the foreman lets it sit.",
 "Grant the eight-hour shift.", "Refuse. The quota comes first."),
"quest_labor_relief_02": ("The proposal continues: weekends, because the body needs a day that belongs to it, and the quota can survive two days of silence. The oldest worker has been asked to speak, and he has said I have forgotten what a Sunday is, and sat down, and the room has not called the vote for a while.",
 "The oldest worker says he has forgotten what a Sunday is, and sits down, and the room does not call the vote for a while.",
 "Give the weekends back.", "Refuse. The curve does not rest."),
"quest_labor_relief_03": ("The proposal is modest this time: one rest day in seven, for the crews that have not had one since the first winter, and the proposal has listed the crews, and the list is most of them, and the room has noticed, because the room is most of them.",
 "The crew list is read, and the list is most of the room, and the room notices, because the room is most of it.",
 "Grant the rest days.", "Refuse. One day costs one day."),
"quest_labor_relief_04": ("The proposal has reached for something the shelter has not had: holidays, because the calendar is a thing people live inside, and the shelter has been living inside the quota's calendar instead, and the proposal asks for three days a year, and names them, and the names are from before, and the room has gone still at the names.",
 "Three holidays are named, and the names are from before, and the room goes still, because the room remembers before.",
 "Give the shelter its holidays.", "Refuse. The calendar is full."),
"quest_labor_relief_05": ("The proposal is practical: sick leave, paid, because the shelter has been paying for sickness anyway, in fevers spread and wounds reopened, and the arithmetic is presented, and the arithmetic favors the sick, which surprises nobody who has watched the infirmary. The vote is called, and it is not close.",
 "The arithmetic is presented, and it favors the sick, and nobody who has watched the infirmary is surprised, and the vote is called.",
 "Grant sick leave, paid.", "Refuse. The sick can rest unpaid."),
"quest_labor_relief_06": ("The proposal names something the shelter has been afraid to name: the children coming, and the mothers carrying them, and the rest owed to both. The proposal is short, and the room has read it twice, and the women in the room have looked at each other, and the vote has passed, and the room has let itself breathe.",
 "The proposal is short, and the room reads it twice, and the vote passes, and the room lets itself breathe.",
 "Grant the mothers their time.", "Refuse. The shelter cannot afford it."),
"quest_labor_relief_07": ("The proposal is the one nobody has argued with: bereavement time, because the dead are owed it and the living need it, and the shelter has been burying its dead on the way to the shift. The proposal asks for three days, and the room has asked for five, and the proposal has been amended, and the vote has not needed to be called.",
 "The proposal asks three days, and the room asks five, and the proposal is amended, and nobody objects.",
 "Grant five days.", "Refuse. The dead can wait for the living's work."),
"quest_labor_relief_08": ("The proposal has used a phrase from before, mental health days, and the room has gone quiet, because the phrase is a luxury, and the shelter has not had luxuries, and the proposal has waited, and then read the infirmary's other list, the one without wounds, and the list is long, and the room has stopped calling it luxury.",
 "The infirmary's other list is read, the one without wounds, and the list is long, and the room stops calling the phrase luxury.",
 "Grant the days.", "Refuse. The mind can wait."),
"quest_labor_relief_09": ("The proposal is the strangest one yet: art and culture shifts, because the shelter has been keeping bodies alive, and the proposal asks what for, and the room has bristled, and the proposal has waited, and then someone has said my daughter has forgotten how to sing, and the bristling has stopped, and the vote has been called.",
 "Someone says her daughter has forgotten how to sing, and the bristling stops, and the vote is called.",
 "Give the shelter its art.", "Refuse. Art comes after survival."),
"quest_labor_relief_10": ("The final proposal is the one the room has not known it was waiting for: absolute leisure, for the exhausted, because the exhausted are the shelter's foundation, and foundations crack. The proposal asks for a week, and the room has asked for two, and the proposal has been amended, and the vote has passed, and nobody has moved to leave, because leaving would mean it was real.",
 "The proposal has passed, and nobody moves to leave, because leaving would mean it is real, and the room sits with that.",
 "Grant the week. And the second.", "Refuse. The shelter runs on the exhausted."),
# ── transparent_truth: the PA says what is true ──
"quest_transparent_truth_01": ("The dwellers deserve to know, and the proposal is on the table: broadcast the truth about the food shortage over the PA, because the shelter has been guessing at the shortfall, and guessing is worse than knowing. The proposal is one paragraph, and the paragraph has the number in it, and the number is real.",
 "The paragraph is read aloud, and the number is in it, and the room has heard the number, and the microphone is on the table.",
 "Broadcast the number.", "Refuse. Panic costs more."),
"quest_transparent_truth_02": ("The broadcast continues: the water shortage, because the aquifer is a fact and the shelter has been drinking around it. The proposal says to say the word aquifer and the word years in the same sentence, and the room has listened to the sentence, and the sentence is true, and the room has let it be true.",
 "The sentence with aquifer and years in it is read aloud, and the room listens, and the sentence is true, and the room lets it be true.",
 "Say it. Broadcast it.", "Refuse. The word years is too much."),
"quest_transparent_truth_03": ("The broadcast reaches the filters: the degradation is a schedule, and the schedule is known, and the shelter has been breathing around the knowledge. The proposal says to post the schedule, in the open, where the shelter can see the date, and the room has looked at the date, and the date is not far, and the room has not looked away.",
 "The filter schedule is posted, and the date is on it, and the room looks at the date, and the date is not far, and the room does not look away.",
 "Post the schedule.", "Refuse. The date will keep."),
"quest_transparent_truth_04": ("The broadcast is hardest this time: the reactor decay, because the reactor is the shelter's heart, and the heart is slowing, and the proposal says to say so, over the PA, in the engineer's words, because the engineer has written them herself, and has asked to read them herself, and the room has let her.",
 "The engineer stands at the microphone with her own words, and the room has let her read them, and she has.",
 "Let her speak.", "Refuse. The heart can slow quietly."),
"quest_transparent_truth_05": ("The broadcast reaches the room itself: leadership mistakes, because the shelter has been governed by people, and people err, and the errors have cost. The proposal lists the errors, and the room has read the list, and the room has signed the list, because the room is the list, and the microphone is waiting.",
 "The list of errors is read, and the room signs it, because the room is the list, and the microphone waits.",
 "Broadcast the confession.", "Refuse. The shelter needs its leaders whole."),
"quest_transparent_truth_06": ("The broadcast reaches the outside: the surface horrors, because the shelter has been imagining the surface, and the imagination is worse, or better, or neither, and the truth is what the scouts have seen. The proposal says to let the scouts speak, and the scouts have been asked, and one has stood up, and the room has waited.",
 "One scout stands up, and the room waits, and the microphone is on, and the scout looks at the room a long time before speaking.",
 "Let the scouts speak.", "Refuse. The surface stays outside."),
"quest_transparent_truth_07": ("The broadcast is the one nobody has wanted to propose: the impossibility of survival, because the arithmetic has been done, and the arithmetic does not end well, and the shelter has been living around the arithmetic. The proposal says to say it, and the room has gone quiet, because the room has known, and the knowing has been the quiet.",
 "The proposal says to say it, and the room goes quiet, because the room has known, and the knowing has been the quiet.",
 "Say it. All of it.", "Refuse. The shelter needs the not-knowing."),
"quest_transparent_truth_08": ("The broadcast reaches the names: the casualty list, because the dead have been counted, and the count has not been read aloud, and the proposal says to read it, over the PA, slowly, and the room has listened to the list being read, and the list has taken a long time, and the room has stayed for all of it.",
 "The casualty list is read over the PA, slowly, and it takes a long time, and the room stays for all of it.",
 "Read every name.", "Refuse. The names can stay counted."),
"quest_transparent_truth_09": ("The broadcast is last this time: the true mathematical doom, because the shelter has been guessing at the end, and the end has a number, and the number has been computed, and the proposal says to post the number, and let the shelter look at it, because the shelter has earned the looking. The room has looked, and the number is real, and the room has not looked away.",
 "The number is posted, and the room looks, and the number is real, and the room does not look away.",
 "Post the number.", "Refuse. The number can wait."),
"quest_transparent_truth_10": ("The final proposal is a principle, and the principle is the shelter's now: total unvarnished honesty, because the shelter has been built on what it knows, and what it knows is the truth, and the truth is what the PA is for. The proposal is one line, and the line is we say what is true, and the room has voted, and the vote has been the shelter's.",
 "One line is posted by the PA: we say what is true, and the room has voted, and the vote has been the shelter's.",
 "Say what is true. Always.", "Refuse. The shelter needs its quiet."),
}
